lotr.waypoint.YELLOW_MIDDLE.info=A wide terrace in the middle of the Yellow Mountains, from where both the coast and the dense jungle in the interior of the mainland are visible. Here lie the remains of the ancient road of the Númenóreans - carved slabs and a tablet with worn runes that has floated over time.
lotr.waypoint.YELLOW_MIDDLE=Miran-Dur
lotr.waypoint.YELLOW_NORTH.info=A lonely rocky spire by the sea, where the lighthouse of Numenor once stood, long extinguished. Used as an observation post for caravans.
lotr.waypoint.YELLOW_NORTH=Arzul-Dun
lotr.waypoint.FALAMAR_SOUTH.info=Tower of Dusk, the last northwestern fortress of Numenor, built in the land of eternal winter and ice. Here, harsh winds from the sea mixed with frosty fogs, and the waters off the coast never melted. The tower stood on a frozen cliff and served as the last beacon for ships heading south. It is said that even after the Fall of Númenor, its icy spire still rises from beneath the ice, like a frozen memory of the end of the age of seafarers.
lotr.waypoint.FALAMAR_SOUTH=Minas-Falmar
lotr.waypoint.ANURION_NORTH.info=Tower of Dawn, the first stronghold of the Numenoreans on the northern shores of the Dark Lands. Here Westerners first set foot on the new continent as the sun rose over the sea. The tower was built of white stone, and its top shone with the copper light of the sunrise. The place was considered the sacred beginning of their expansion and a symbol of the awakening of light in unfamiliar lands.
lotr.waypoint.ANURION_NORTH=Minas Aurion
lotr.waypoint.TAURWAITH_NORTH.info=Here is the capital of Taurwait, taken from the local savages and rebuilt from scratch, where from now on the main attribute was precious stones, which the locals called “bringers of doom” because of how brightly they sparkled before the decorated blades cut the throats of the enemies of the jungle people.
lotr.waypoint.TAURWAITH_NORTH=Ilong Kuah
lotr.waypoint.TAURWAITH_SOUTH.info=the city of Taurwait, built on one side along the river. According to stories, it was founded by an ancient leader who once saw thousands of scarlet stones strewn along the bottom of the river, but no matter how hard he tried, he could not take them all.
lotr.waypoint.TAURWAITH_SOUTH=Eyeka Kuah
lotr.waypoint.MOREDAIN_NORTH.info=A tribe of savages, long separated from their southern relatives, is located here. The continuous, surprise attacks from Taurwhaite kept them from recovering, but made it clear that they needed a new leader. Many of them were killed and eaten by their own people, as they were considered too weak
lotr.waypoint.MOREDAIN_NORTH=Mor'Nahu
lotr.waypoint.MOREDAIN_SOUTH.info=Here live the ancestors of those who refused to sail west with the great leader, but chose to continue the war with the jungle people in revenge for their relatives.
lotr.waypoint.MOREDAIN_SOUTH=Mor’Dahu
